{{examples-right|sense=rhetoric|examples=''She lowered her standards by raising her glass, Her courage, her eyes and his hopes.''<br>- Flanders and Swan<br>He ''[[slipped]]'' on his jacket and a banana peel.<br>She ''[[crib]]bed'' the baby and (then) the corn.<br>She ''came'' in high spirits and a Cadillac.<br>"The man who has never ''[[made]]'' a mistake will never ''make'' anything else" ([[w:George Bernard Shaw|George Bernard Shaw]]).}}
# {{rhetoric}} A [[figure of speech]] in which one [[word]] [[simultaneously]] [[modifies]] two or more other words such that the modification must be [[understood]] [[differently]] with respect to each modified word; often causing [[humorous]] [[incongruity]]
# {{botany}} [[growth|Growth]] in which [[lateral]] [[branch]]es develop from a lateral [[meristem]], without the formation of a [[bud]] or period of [[dormancy]], when the lateral meristem is split from a [[terminal]] meristem.

